Rule 2 (all elements in the axis tuple must be within valid range for the input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0 - ndim(v_1) ∧ v_2[i] < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 3 (all elements in the axis list must be within valid range for the input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0 - ndim(v_1) ∧ v_2[i] < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 5 (all elements in the axis tuple must be within the valid range for the input tensor and tuple length must not exceed tensor rank)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= v_2.len ≤ ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0 - ndim(v_1) ∧ v_2[i] < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 6 (all elements in the axis list must be within the valid range for the input tensor and list length must not exceed tensor rank)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= v_2.len ≤ ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0 - ndim(v_1) ∧ v_2[i] < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 7 (for 1-D tensor, the axis must be 0 or -1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then v_2 = 0 ∨ v_2 = -1
>>
Rule 8 (axes specified as a tuple must be unique and the tuple length cannot exceed the tensor rank)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ v_2.len ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : if i ≠ j then v_2[i] ≠ v_2[j]
>>
Rule 9 (axes specified as a list must be unique and the list length cannot exceed the tensor rank)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ v_2.len ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : if i ≠ j then v_2[i] ≠ v_2[j]
>>
Rule 10 (for an integer axis, the index must be within the positive or negative bounds of the tensor dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 < 0 then v_2 ≥ 0 - ndim(v_1) else v_2 < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 11 (when axes are specified as a tuple, the number of specified axes must not exceed the number of dimensions of the tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= v_2.len ≤ ndim(v_1)
